#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# heun_b

#% text
# `heun_b(q, alpha, gamma, delta, epsilon, z)` gives the biconfluent Heun function, the solution of the biconfluent Heun equation that is analytic at 0 with value 1.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The equation is `z y'' + (gamma + delta z + epsilon z^2) y' + (alpha z - q) y = 0`: a regular singularity at 0 and an irregular one at infinity.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values: the series at the normalization point and analytic continuation by Taylor series along the segment to `z`, around the singularities on the upper side (values on the cuts are the limits from above).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
heun_b(-0.2, 1.3, 0.12, -0.14, 4.32, -0.3)
#% output
#= 1.4180011084243804

#% cell
n(heun_b(9/10, -14/10, 12/100, 3/100, -2/10, 1/10), 30)
#% output
#= 1.787802431349323542867771685382054

#% cell
heun_b(1.2, -1.4, 0.12, 0.03, -0.2, [0.15, 0.1 + im, im, 4])
#% output
#= [2.6442328202310676, -3.6600857070164987 + 7.652933556741085im, -3.7800476761712347 + 6.818763441973563im, 2962.23012751039]

